Resilience refers to the ability of a system to continue operating despite failures, unexpected events, or infrastructure disruptions.

Key resilience strategies include:

* Resource redundancy
* Geographic distribution
* Automatic failover
* Health monitoring
* Backup and recovery
* Fault isolation

# Real-Life Example:
For example, an airline reservation platform may replicate services across multiple Azure regions so that travellers can continue booking flights even if one datacentre becomes unavailable.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is healthcare systems ensuring uninterrupted access to patient records during regional infrastructure failures.

Resilient architectures improve customer trust and minimise operational disruption during unexpected incidents.
